          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Jane and Jacqui each think of a number. The number Jane thinks of is twice Jacqui’s number and the sum of the two numbers is 39. What numbers did they think of?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Jane: $26$; Jacqui: $13$.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be Jane’s number and $y$ be Jacqui’s number.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=2y &&(1)\\\\x+y&=39 &&(2)\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute equation (1) into equation (2):\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2y+y&=39\\\\3y&=39\\\\y&=13\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute $y=13$ into equation (1):\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=2\\times13\\\\x&=26\\end{align*}$$\n\nJane thought of $26$ and Jacqui thought of $13$.\n\nCheck: $26=2\\times13$ and $26+13=39$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
